\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. O Son of Man, our hero strong and tender,
\par Whose servants are the brave in all the earth,
\par Our living sacrifice to Thee we render,
\par Who sharest all our sorrows, all our mirth.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. O feet so strong to climb the path of duty,
\par O lips divine that taught the words of truth,
\par Kind eyes that marked the lilies in their beauty,
\par And heart that kindled at the zeal of  youth.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Lover of children, boyhood's inspiration,
\par Of all mankind the servant and the king;
\par O Lord of joy and hope and consolation,
\par To Thee our fears and joys and hopes we bring.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Not in our failures only and our sadness
\par We seek Thy presence, Comforter and Friend;
\par O rich man's Guest, be with us in our gladness,
\par O poor man's Mate, our lowliest tasks attend
\par 
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

